A||||7||Axmanmkii||Another newbie question||||1||
Z||000000||Axmanmkii||12-28-2001||02:01 PM||||I notice alot of you work on your own cars. <P>My really quick question is, how did you learn? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-28-2001||02:07 PM||||A lot of members here are "natural born mechanics"...<P>Myself, I was never into cars until I purchased my Fiero. I bought manuals, read ALOT, and asked questions here at the forum.   <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/compute.gif"> <P>I found a neighbor who had a Fiero also. He's given me support as well..<P>I find that I ENJOY and WANT to work on my Fiero, so I'll try it myself before I have work done by someone else.<P>It's just one of those things..<P>The people on this forum are just amazing!!!! I probably would of sold my Fiero if I didn't find the knowledge and support that is here!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.btinternet.co.uk/sm/notworthy.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">      <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||12-28-2001||02:16 PM||||I'm certainly not one of the "natural born mechanics" around here.  I just have a lot of stuff in my head <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. And I've learned my limits... and also learned that when fixing/working on stuff- having a backup daily driver is a must!  I can handle the basics... and next year I'm going to jump into bodywork!  But if I can't easily see the solution- then my Dad (& my Brother) are both "naturals" and they help me out!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||12-28-2001||02:24 PM||||Here's a website that I've found has helped me a lot...<P> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <P>Wait for it to fully load and scroll down.<BR>Lot's of good info!!!<P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">     <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||12-28-2001||02:25 PM||||just ask here how to do it and get a Haynes or Chilton service manual from parts store for about $15. Be surprised how much you learn just tinkering.<P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/rogergarrison1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||88CoupeV6||12-28-2001||07:07 PM||||I have always loved working on cars. The fiero is also a very easy car to work on. Once you know what you are doing they are simple to fix. For me anyway. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Lucky6_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||avengador1||12-28-2001||07:12 PM||||I learned from my father. He used to race when I was a little boy, and I would watch him work on his car. I also had a class in high school and went to college to become a Mechanial Engineer. I've been working on my own cars since I was 16 now Im 42. You learn by watching, practicing, and helping others work on their cars.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||JayLT1||12-29-2001||02:07 AM||||i have to agree with most of these guys, read alot and ask questions, im also taking a auto tech class so that helps too.  And trust me if you dont get it ask someone who does, parts are expensive to fix if you break them. <BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86 Black GT (95LT1 on the way)||||reg||1
